[step] The 0.300 mm separation is the depth of an outer station-witness recess in the rear face, not a 0.300 mm wall. Each recess is 0.8 mm wide at Y48.1..48.9 or its negative twin and 3 mm high at print Z12..15. Its inner edge is 1.1 mm outside the nominal diameter-30 mm clamp-pad bearing disk. The analytic STEP retains the complete 12 mm stock below the recess and continuous wing stock from X8 to the recess floor at X38.2. Both nominal pad disks retain flat, uninterrupted rear bearing faces.
alternatives: An ink-only witness removes the shallow recess without changing the force path, but must be renewed after cleaning. Deepening the recess consumes wing stock; widening it toward the pad reduces the current 1.1 mm separation from the nominal bearing disk. The current detail is a blind witness cut outside that disk.
