[thin] The 1.100 mm minima are the outer margins beside the two shallow rear-face witness grooves: Y48.9..50 and the negative twin. Each margin projects only 0.3 mm beyond the X38.2 groove floor over the upper 3 mm of the 15 mm half-jaw; the analytic STEP retains a complete 12 mm of stock below that footprint and 30.2 mm of continuous wing stock inward from the groove floor to X8. The nominal diameter-30 mm pad-bearing disks end at Y47 or -47, leaving 1.1 mm to the grooves' inner edges. These short witness margins do not describe full-height 1.1 mm wing webs. This dimensional description supplies no as-printed strength or life rating.
alternatives: Removing the grooves and marking only with ink removes their narrow outer margins without enlarging the load-bearing disk, but requires renewing the marks after cleaning. Widening the wings increases the outer margin but adds stock beyond the nominal pad envelope. Moving either groove inward consumes its current separation from the pad-bearing disk.
